{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Finite","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.DegreeSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.binding_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.binding_pos","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L107-L113","doc":"Given the conditional class with a strictly positive per-bond energy, the\nbinding energy is strictly positive once there is at least one bond (`2 ≤ A`,\nso `C(A,2) > 0`). Sharpens `binding_nonneg` on the coordinated regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.binding_eq_zero_of_lt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.binding_eq_zero_of_lt_two","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L100-L105","doc":"Given the conditional class, the binding vanishes below two nucleons: with\nfewer than two nucleons there are no bonds (`C(A,2) = 0`), so the extensive\nbinding is exactly zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.two_mul_binding_eq_epsilon_sum_degrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.two_mul_binding_eq_epsilon_sum_degrees","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L84-L98","doc":"**Coordination bridge: `2·B = ε · ∑_v z(A)`.** Twice the (conditional)\nextensive binding energy equals the per-bond energy times the summed\ncoordination degrees `∑_v deg v`. This is the machine-checked combinatorial\ncertificate the file's purpose calls for: it routes the binding law's bond\ncount through the proved handshake identity (`coordination_handshake`) rather\nthan through the bare `A.choose 2`, so the extensivity is tied to the actual\nper-nucleon coordination degrees. Still fully conditional on\n`BondExtensiveBinding` — it certifies the *shape* of the law against the graph,\nit does not assert the law holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.binding_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.binding_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L79-L82","doc":"Given the conditional class, the binding energy is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.binding_eq_bond_energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.binding_eq_bond_energy","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L74-L77","doc":"Given the conditional class, the binding energy equals the per-bond energy times the\nbond count. (Just `h.extensive`, exposed as a named consumer.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.extensive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.extensive","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L72-L72","doc":"OPEN hypothesis: binding is extensive in the bond count `C(A,2)` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.epsilon_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.epsilon_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L70-L70","doc":"per-bond energy is non-negative ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.binding","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L68-L68","doc":"the many-body binding energy of the `A`-nucleon cluster ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.epsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.epsilon","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L66-L66","doc":"per-bond binding energy (archimedean, ℝ) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.BondExtensiveBinding","kind":"structure","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L58-L72","doc":"**Conditional extensive-binding class (the OPEN input, not derived).** Asserts that the\nmany-body binding energy of the `A`-nucleon cluster is `ε` per nucleon–nucleon bond times the\nbond count `C(A,2)`, with a non-negative per-bond energy `ε`. The field `extensive` is the\narc's open hypothesis (`b_αα`-type per-bond constant is empirical, not from the 13 drivers);\nthis class carries it so downstream facts are verified *conditional on it*, never asserting it\nholds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.coordination_handshake","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.coordination_handshake","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L52-L56","doc":"**Handshake identity.** Summing the per-nucleon coordination degree over all `A` nucleons\ndouble-counts every bond: `∑_v deg v = 2 · C(A,2)`. Ties the two counts above together. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.bond_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.bond_count","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L46-L50","doc":"**Total nucleon–nucleon bond count `C(A,2)`.** The number of edges of the\nfully-coordinated cluster on `A` nucleons is `A.choose 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.coordination_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBinding.coordination_degree","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBinding.lean#L39-L44","doc":"**Per-nucleon coordination number `z(A) = A − 1`.** In the fully-coordinated cluster of\n`A` nucleons — the complete graph `⊤ : SimpleGraph (Fin A)` — every nucleon is bonded to the\nother `A − 1`, i.e. its degree is `A − 1`. This is the topological integer the arc identifies\nwith the open-shell multiplier `M(open shell)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}